	"name": "Reinforced Cane",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/weapons/staves/staff-simple-gold.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>While most canes are shod in iron or other metals to protect the wooden core from splintering or otherwised being damaged by the stones one walks upon, the reinforced cane is not only shod, but girded.</p><p>Bands of metal run up the sides of a reinforced cane from the foot all the way to the handle in order to provide significant additional strength to the tool itself.</p><p>When used as a bludgeoning weapon, a reinforced cane mostly strikes upon the metal inlays that protect the core, and strikes with a notable weight. However some reinforced canes can deal piercing damage if they have an ice-foot. Ice-feet do not cost extra to be built into a reinforced cane, and grant advantage on saving throws to avoid slipping due to a surface being icy or slippery. However they tend to be hell on wood flooring.</p>",
